title: Card effects and a computer opponent
intro: Cards that deal damage, heal and cost mana, aimed at what you choose, and a computer that plays its hand against you, all with no code.
project: Empty | Card Duel

chapter: Cards that do things | Card Effect
create: Deck
select: Hand
set: Hand.StartWith = 0
set: Hand.MaxMana = 3
explain: field:Hand.MaxMana | Mana | A hand has mana to pay for its cards, three here. It fills back up as each of its side's turns starts.
create: Card
rename: Fireball
add: Card Effect
set: CardEffect.Damage = 3
set: Card.Cost = 2
explain: component:CardEffect | Card Effect | A card effect says what a card does when it's played: damage, healing, drawing, making the opponent discard, mana, a buff, or any action in the scene. This one deals three damage to the opponent, and the card costs two mana.
select: Hand
create: Card
rename: Zap
add: Card Effect
set: CardEffect.Target = Chosen
set: CardEffect.Damage = 1
set: Card.Cost = 1
explain: field:CardEffect.Target | Target | Its target is the opponent, yourself, every foe, every friend, everyone, or one the player chooses as they play it. Zap hits whatever it's aimed at.
select: Hand
create: Card
rename: Potion
add: Card Effect
set: CardEffect.Target = Self
set: CardEffect.Heal = 4
deselect
create: Text
rename: Enemy Hero
set: Transform.Position.X = -6.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = 3.4
set: Text.Size = 0.45
add: Health
set: Health.Max = 20
set: Text.Track = Enemy Hero
set: Text.Output = Health
set: Text.Value = Enemy {0}
explain: component:Health | The opponent | The opponent is anything with health: here a text that shows how much it has left.

chapter: Playing them | Drag, aim, pay
play
wait: 1
gamedrag: Fireball > Play Zone
wait: 0.6
expectvalue: Enemy Hero.Health.Current = 17
expectvalue: Hand.Hand.Mana = 1
explain: game | Played | Fireball deals three damage and takes two of the hand's three mana. A card the hand can't pay for shows its cost dimmed and stays in the hand.
gamedrag: Zap > Play Zone
wait: 0.4
say: Zap waits to be aimed: a line runs from it to the mouse. Click what it should hit.
gameclick: Enemy Hero
wait: 0.6
expectvalue: Enemy Hero.Health.Current = 16
expectvalue: Hand.Hand.Mana = 0
expectvalue: Zap.Card.PlayedBy = Hand
stop

chapter: A computer opponent | Turn Order
create: Text
rename: Turns
set: Transform.Position.X = 6.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = 3.4
set: Text.Size = 0.4
add: Turn Order
set: TurnOrder.ComputerTurnTime = 0
explain: component:TurnOrder | Turns | A turn order: the player's turn, then the enemy's, which the computer plays.
create: Text
rename: Player Hero
set: Transform.Position.X = -6.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2.4
set: Text.Size = 0.45
add: Health
set: Health.Max = 20
set: Text.Track = Player Hero
set: Text.Output = Health
set: Text.Value = You {0}
add: Turn Taker
select: Enemy Hero
add: Turn Taker
set: TurnTaker.Side = Enemy
select: Hand
add: Turn Taker
key: Ctrl+D
rename: Enemy Hand
set: Transform.Position.Y = 4.4
set: TurnTaker.Side = Enemy
set: Hand.Hidden = true
explain: component:Hand | The computer's hand | A copy of the hand, on the enemy's side and hidden. A hand on a side the computer plays is played by the computer on its turn.
explain: field:Hand.ThinkTime | Think Time | It thinks before each play, and shows the card it's about to play lifted out of its hand so you can follow. It finishes you off when it can, heals when its hero is low, and otherwise plays the most damage it can pay for, keeping its healing for later.
play
wait: 1
gamedrag: Fireball > Play Zone
wait: 0.6
expectvalue: Enemy Hero.Health.Current = 17
tap: Tab
wait: 0.4
explain: game | Its turn | Your turn ends with Tab. The computer shows its fireball, plays it at you, then aims its zap at you too, and keeps its potion.
wait: 3
expectvalue: Player Hero.Health.Current = 16
expectvalue: Turns.TurnOrder.Current = Player
expectvalue: Hand.Hand.Mana = 3
say: Its mana spent and nothing it wants to play, it ends its turn, and your mana fills back up.
stop
say: That's card effects with no code: damage, healing, draws, discards, mana and any action, aimed where you choose, and a computer that plays its hand by a rule you can follow, the same way every time in a seeded game.
